      "message": "let\u0027s add a print (that is always printed) with the new frequency and the results of the call.\n\nAlso, can we only perform this operation if it is changing?\nWe might need a get frequency too.\n\nAlso, we should only allow this on ports that have explicitly opted into run-time frequency change. Let\u0027s make a new flag that we use in i2c_port_t.kpbs field like \n\n#define I2C_DYNAMIC_SPEED BIT(31)\n\nand then config struct\n\n.kbps \u003d I2C_DYNAMIC_SPEED | 400 /* 400 is initial speed */\n\n\nAnd if the config doesn\u0027t have I2C_DYNAMIC_SPEED, then we fail to change the i2c bus speed",
